      "writtenOn": "2021-01-14T19:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding extensible, it\u0027s true you don\u0027t need to change telephony manager API if you want to add one more param in the future, but all the caller still needs an update when they create a SignalStrengthUpdateRequest, right? SignalStrengthUpdateRequest is also a public API and you\u0027ll still have to deprecate the old constructor. Unless you use a Builder model for SignalStrengthUpdateRequest.",
      "parentUuid": "5182f9a6_c693faec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "255e1b76abf2a288024c3128c6f8c44824eb2a38",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70aadaaa_590d3135",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/SignalStrengthUpdateRequest.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-14T20:24:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can\u0027t send the \"inner\" parameters directly via TelephonyManager method though (at least with the current shape). We need place for the caller to hold onto a reference that can later be used to unregister the request. Having a wrapper object gives us a way to do that. The alternative shape would still require an object, but if could be \"returned\"... that still doesn\u0027t save us the object though.\n\nSignalStrengthToken token \u003d TM#registerRequest(SignalStrengthThresholdInfos, shouldReport...)\n\nTM#unregisterRequest(token)\n\nHence, a builder here would be nice.",
      "parentUuid": "dbc93184_b2249cd9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "255e1b76abf2a288024c3128c6f8c44824eb2a38",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
